& [SelectedIntention] is the next dependency-ready runtime frontier
  + [original_intention] is a Cantor-hosted Shaliach manager engages Codex and purpose-scoped Cantors to build the ecosystem through inspectable messages and responses
  + [continuation_authority] is the preserved four-hour instruction to continue productive in-scope Cantor work through successive governed slices
  + [phase_selection] is phase_3_scoped_write from the signed supervised ecosystem runtime formation
  + [required_outcome] is one Codex turn may eventually change only an isolated candidate workspace and return a sealed candidate, tests, and proof for independent review

& [DelineationFinding] is Phase 3 contains four different authority transitions
  + [Phase3A_CandidateWorkspaceAdmission] is read-only verification of an operator-prepared isolated Git worktree, exact base, exact branch, clean baseline, path policy, tool identity, and resource budgets
  + [Phase3B_BoundedCandidateMutation] is one workspace-write Codex turn confined to the admitted disposable worktree with no network, no approval, no repository-history mutation, and no authority outside the candidate
  + [Phase3C_CandidateSealAndReview] is deterministic capture of changed paths, bytes, tests, event evidence, and independent Observer judgment over an immutable result capsule
  + [Phase3D_GovernedPromotion] is a separate human or separately commissioned EffectBroker operation that may sign, commit, merge, push, activate, migrate, or roll back
  = must: assign a separate state transition and proof boundary to each phase
  - never: infer promotion authority from permission to modify a disposable candidate workspace

& [FirstActivationBoundary] is Phase3A only
  + [inside] is strict data forms, exact executable and path admission, bounded read-only Git inspection, clean and isolated worktree proof, deterministic admission receipt, staleness check, adversarial fixtures, documentation, and evidence
  + [outside] is creating, moving, deleting, resetting, cleaning, or modifying a worktree; starting a workspace-write model turn; running candidate tests; sealing a changed candidate; staging, committing, merging, pushing, signing, activating, deploying, or promoting anything
  + [reason] is the write target must be proven disposable and bounded before any writer can be pointed at it
  - never: treat this source selection as raw user dictation or as implementation authority for Phase3B through Phase3D

& [SafetyInterpretation] is explicit
  + [candidate_mutation] is a contained local effect, not a semantic observation
  + [candidate_workspace] is not the principal working tree and is not current runtime authority
  + [review] is performed from a fresh immutable capsule, not from model claims
  + [promotion] remains locked even when mutation and review eventually pass
  + [rollback] for Phase3A is removal or non-use of the read-only admission module with no repository state to undo
